{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/845308-monster-by-skillet-perfect-theme-song-for-beast","id":845308,"title":"Monster by Skillet: Perfect theme song for Beast?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-10T15:19:11-08:00","id":845308,"title":"Monster by Skillet: Perfect theme song for Beast?","content":"As I said in the Title, is Monster by Skillet the perfect theme song for Beast: The Primordial?<br /> <br /> Maybe even the Chronicles Of Darkness as a whole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T17:38:08-08:00","id":845371,"title":"","content":"Nope. For Beast, you want You Should Know Where I'm Coming From by Banks. Harder to pin one for ChroD, but I quite like Liquid Man by Theatre of Tragedy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T20:44:45-08:00","id":845421,"title":"","content":"Nah, Monster is the perfect theme song for Werewolf.<br /> <br /> For Beast, you have Sister Sledge's &quot;We Are Family&quot; (from their perspective) and Creature Feature's &quot;Mommy's Little Monsters&quot; (from the perspective of everyone else). Creature Feature is Beastly as all get-out.<br /> <br /> The wisdom through fear aspect has too many angles to properly cover with one song. I'm fond of the Hunger For Punishment, so I suggest the following: Abney Park's &quot;Victorian Vigilante&quot;, Arthur Brown's &quot;Fire&quot;, Johnny Cash's &quot;God's Gonna Cut You Down&quot;, Miracle Of Sound's &quot;I Am The Night&quot;, Queen's &quot;Another One Bites The Dust&quot;, Ben Moody &amp; Anastacia's &quot;Everything Burns&quot;, Nico Vega's &quot;Fury Oh Fury&quot; and Lordi's &quot;Rock Police&quot;. I'll stop here because there are far too many awesome songs about revenge out there.<br /> <br /> And if you ever feel like just enjoying your monstrosity for once, you might like Lord Dominator's &quot;I'm The Bad Guy&quot; (Wander Over Yonder), The Joker's &quot;Where's The Fun In That&quot; (Batman: The Brave And The Bold), Voltaire's &quot;When You're Evil&quot;, Lordi's &quot;Monster Is My Name&quot; and the Boogie Song from The Nightmare Before Christmas.<br /> <br /> EDIT: By the way, Lordi is just as Beastly as Creature Feature. I heartily recommend them. A lot of their songs are about something mundane turned monstrous, from grannies to presidents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-11-2016, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.